Review of PR #2543 (ADR 0052, docs-only — two files, 199 new lines). The ADR's claims were checked against the codebase (`expectation_allowlist.py`, `datasources/monitors.py`, `services/custom_sql.py`, `services/schema_drift.py`, `db/models.py`) and against the live ODCS v3.0.2 and v3.2 specifications. All ten findings were posted as inline comments on the PR (ids 4369924251–4369924698).

```json
[
  {
    "file": "docs/site/adr/0052-data-contracts-odcs.md",
    "line": 111,
    "summary": "§5 accepts apiVersion v3.0.0–v3.2.0, but the §3 mapping keys only on v3.1+ `metric` names and `{object}` placeholders; v3.0.x documents use `rule: duplicateCount/validValues/rowCount` and `${object}`/`${property}`.",
    "failure_scenario": "A v3.0.2 contract imports 'successfully' with every library clause in `unmapped` and every sql rule refused by the validator because `${object}` was never substituted — the rollup reads 'not enforced' for a contract DataQ claims to support."
  },
  {
    "file": "docs/site/adr/0052-data-contracts-odcs.md",
    "line": 84,
    "summary": "`rowCount` → `volume` has no encoding for a one-sided rule: monitors.py requires integer `min_rows` AND `max_rows` with max >= min.",
    "failure_scenario": "`rowCount mustBeGreaterThan: 1000` forces the importer to invent a `max_rows` the producer never wrote (fires on normal growth) or to send the clause to `unmapped`; the ADR says neither."
  },
  {
    "file": "docs/site/adr/0052-data-contracts-odcs.md",
    "line": 86,
    "summary": "`SELECT 1 WHERE NOT ((<query>) <op>)` passes when the scalar subquery is NULL.",
    "failure_scenario": "Empty table / `SUM` over no rows → `NOT (NULL > 5)` is NULL → zero unexpected rows → a breached `mustBeGreaterThan` rule reports pass."
  },
  {
    "file": "docs/site/adr/0052-data-contracts-odcs.md",
    "line": 76,
    "summary": "`exclusiveMinimum`/`exclusiveMaximum`/`multipleOf` from `logicalTypeOptions` have no table row; `expect_column_values_to_be_between` needs `strict_min`/`strict_max`.",
    "failure_scenario": "A property with `exclusiveMaximum: 100` is either silently dropped (contradicting 'never drops a clause silently') or mapped inclusive, admitting the exact boundary value the contract forbids."
  },
  {
    "file": "docs/site/adr/0052-data-contracts-odcs.md",
    "line": 89,
    "summary": "SLA `frequency` → `max_age_hours = value` breaches on every healthy refresh cycle; frequency is cadence, not a staleness ceiling.",
    "failure_scenario": "Daily-refreshed table, `max_age_hours = 24`: any run landing minutes after the 24h boundary (beat jitter, run scheduled before the load) fails freshness on a healthy feed — a permanently flapping check."
  },
  {
    "file": "docs/site/adr/0052-data-contracts-odcs.md",
    "line": 79,
    "summary": "ODCS `enum` (v3.2.0+) is an array of `{value, label, ...}` objects, not scalars, and does not exist before v3.2.0.",
    "failure_scenario": "Feeding the array straight to `value_set` makes `expect_column_values_to_be_in_set` compare column values against dicts — every row unexpected, the check fails on a conforming column."
  },
  {
    "file": "docs/site/adr/0052-data-contracts-odcs.md",
    "line": 58,
    "summary": "`ON DELETE SET NULL` nulls `contract_id` only; `suites.contract_object` is left dangling.",
    "failure_scenario": "Contract deleted → suite keeps `contract_object='orders'`; a later `PATCH /suites/{id}` setting only `contract_id` to another contract inherits a stale object name and the rollup attributes the wrong clauses to it."
  },
  {
    "file": "docs/site/adr/0052-data-contracts-odcs.md",
    "line": 49,
    "summary": "Unique key `(lower(name), version)` ignores ODCS's required `id` and the stored `domain`/`tenant`.",
    "failure_scenario": "Two producers in different domains both publish `orders` 1.0.0 → second import 409s; a contract renamed but keeping its ODCS `id` is treated as unrelated, so §6's new-version reconciliation never triggers."
  },
  {
    "file": "docs/site/adr/0052-data-contracts-odcs.md",
    "line": 93,
    "summary": "Severity mapping escalates every ODCS level one notch (`info`→`warn`, `warning`→`fail`, absent→`fail`).",
    "failure_scenario": "A producer labels a rule `warning`; DataQ opens an incident and alerts at `fail`. Most ODCS rules carry no severity, so the harshest default applies to the commonest case."
  },
  {
    "file": "docs/site/adr/0052-data-contracts-odcs.md",
    "line": 94,
    "summary": "`schedule`/`scheduler` sit on each quality rule in ODCS, not on the object; 'first cron wins' is document-order dependent.",
    "failure_scenario": "Object with rules at `0 2 * * *` and `0 14 * * *`; a re-import with the rules re-ordered silently swaps the suite's schedule and marks the other `unmapped`."
  }
]
```

Verified-consistent, no finding: `{object}`/`{property}` placeholders match ODCS v3.1+; the five `metric` names match v3.1+; the seven ODCS dimension values are correct; `CHECK_ORIGINS` / `SUITE_ORIGINS` exist in `backend/app/db/models.py:96-97`; every GX expectation named in the table is in `ALLOWED_EXPECTATIONS`; `column_policy.pii_columns` exists; ADR 0016/0037/0047 exist as cited (0016 and 0037 are relied on in the body but missing from the Related header — cosmetic, not posted).

